(4292674, 616541, 61961, '<td valign="top">Hello Aaron.  Congratulations!  You are just the second person to enter a DP Challenge using the new D300! :-)<br/> <br/>I like your photo.  It''s a simple idea, but lovely.  Fits the theme very well, too.<br/> <br/>If I may be hyper-critical, I see three things that could use tweaking.  First, the photo tilts a bit to the right.  If you have the extra space to crop around the subject, you could rotate a bit to the left so the ornament hangs perfectly vertical.  Second, the vignetting on the right side is sort of heavy for this photo.  Third, I think the ornament is a bit soft.  I see you used f/5.6 -- one would think this would be plenty -- but still the focus seems sharper on part of the branch.<br/> <br/>Hope you don''t mind the nitpicking.  I''m anxiously awaiting my D300 and expect there to be a big learning curve.  Keep up the good work! <br/> <br/> - Larry in NYC</td>', 'Hello Aaron.  Congratulations!  You are just the second person to enter a DP Challenge using the new D300! :-) I like your photo.  It''s a simple idea, but lovely.  Fits the theme very well, too. If I may be hyper-critical, I see three things that could use tweaking.  First, the photo tilts a bit to the right.  If you have the extra space to crop around the subject, you could rotate a bit to the left so the ornament hangs perfectly vertical.  Second, the vignetting on the right side is sort of heavy for this photo.  Third, I think the ornament is a bit soft.  I see you used f/5.6 -- one would think this would be plenty -- but still the focus seems sharper on part of the branch. Hope you don''t mind the nitpicking.  I''m anxiously awaiting my D300 and expect there to be a big learning curve.  Keep up the good work!   - Larry in NYC', '2007-12-05 14:48:39.000000', NULL, 0),
