(4307386, 617403, 67697, '<td valign="top">I liked seeing this during the challenge.  The red and green pop out well from the white background.  And the colors, plus the fact that they are beverages, really make for a festive shot.</td>', 'I liked seeing this during the challenge.  The red and green pop out well from the white background.  And the colors, plus the fact that they are beverages, really make for a festive shot.', '2007-12-10 22:52:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4307530, 617100, 29269, '<td valign="top">Vec pokazujes napredak... mislim da su u pravu ovi koji su rekli da je "burned out" - desni cosak i jeste malo ''overexposed'' - ali je zgleda tako moralo biti obzirom na to da sama ruza izgleda korektno osvijetljena. <br/>Kako izbjeci ovo ubuduce? Najjednostavniji nacin je da se zakloni necim izvor svjetla (sunce) na onom presvijetlom dijelu. Alternativa je da se dodatno osvijetli sam objekat, i u isto vrijeme smanji vrijeme ekspozicije. Npr. mozes koristiti blic.<br/> <br/>Druga stvar je nesto sto se zove rule of thirds - a u stvari se radi o zlatnom presjeku. Potrazi malo po interetu (ili u knjigama matematike :-) o tome, pa mozes sam testirati teoriju da je ljudskom oku privlacnije kada se objekti ne nalaze u centru fotografije, nego kad su malo smaknuti (<a href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_ratio" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">link</a>)<br/> <br/>Probaj odrezati donji desni kraj tako da se centar ruze pomjeri prema donjem desnom cosku, oko 1/3 odozdo i s desna, i vidi kako ti se vizuelno cini.<br/> <br/>Sretno ubuduce!<br/> <br/>-Srdjan</td>', 'Vec pokazujes napredak... mislim da su u pravu ovi koji su rekli da je "burned out" - desni cosak i jeste malo ''overexposed'' - ali je zgleda tako moralo biti obzirom na to da sama ruza izgleda korektno osvijetljena. Kako izbjeci ovo ubuduce? Najjednostavniji nacin je da se zakloni necim izvor svjetla (sunce) na onom presvijetlom dijelu. Alternativa je da se dodatno osvijetli sam objekat, i u isto vrijeme smanji vrijeme ekspozicije. Npr. mozes koristiti blic. Druga stvar je nesto sto se zove rule of thirds - a u stvari se radi o zlatnom presjeku. Potrazi malo po interetu (ili u knjigama matematike :-) o tome, pa mozes sam testirati teoriju da je ljudskom oku privlacnije kada se objekti ne nalaze u centru fotografije, nego kad su malo smaknuti (link) Probaj odrezati donji desni kraj tako da se centar ruze pomjeri prema donjem desnom cosku, oko 1/3 odozdo i s desna, i vidi kako ti se vizuelno cini. Sretno ubuduce! -Srdjan', '2007-12-11 00:42:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4307848, 617249, 18011, '<td valign="top">Thank youuuuuu!<br/> <br/>Gipo ;-D</td>', 'Thank youuuuuu! Gipo ;-D', '2007-12-11 07:55:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4308977, 616273, 70036, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>It looks like your commenters put it very well.  This image screams for contrast and color.  There is much potential in this photo but it needs some post processing.  Contrast and saturation would do wonders.  Possibly some sharpening - it is hard to see whether it is in focus or not.<br/> <br/>You seem to have done a good job with a shallow DOF as the background is nicely blurred.  It would be nice to see this image after some procesing.<br/> <br/>Please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Ken<br/>alexzen<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) It looks like your commenters put it very well.  This image screams for contrast and color.  There is much potential in this photo but it needs some post processing.  Contrast and saturation would do wonders.  Possibly some sharpening - it is hard to see whether it is in focus or not. You seem to have done a good job with a shallow DOF as the background is nicely blurred.  It would be nice to see this image after some procesing. Please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Kenalexzen ', '2007-12-11 18:57:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4308988, 617404, 70036, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>This did not score very well so let''s see why.   <br/> <br/>Composition<br/> <br/>It is a centered image which does not help with the drama of the photo. It is not clear that this involves multiple stockings.  My first take was that it was a snapshot of an existing wall hanging.<br/> <br/>A more interesting composition might be to lay the stockings randomly on top of each other while still spelling NOEL.   Create a pattern, make it off center, make a design.<br/> <br/>Lighting<br/> <br/>The lighting is flat which does not help the colors.  Given the objects I am not sure what could be done with the lighting as no shadows are really possible.<br/> <br/>Please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Ken <br/>alexzen<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) This did not score very well so let''s see why.    Composition It is a centered image which does not help with the drama of the photo. It is not clear that this involves multiple stockings.  My first take was that it was a snapshot of an existing wall hanging. A more interesting composition might be to lay the stockings randomly on top of each other while still spelling NOEL.   Create a pattern, make it off center, make a design. Lighting The lighting is flat which does not help the colors.  Given the objects I am not sure what could be done with the lighting as no shadows are really possible. Please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Ken alexzen ', '2007-12-11 19:08:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4309000, 617468, 70036, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>First I commend for trying something out of the box.   A few things that I notice:<br/> <br/>Composition<br/> <br/>The composition is not very interesting.  The line in the middle is not straight and that detracts.  I would straighten the image via crop.   The lights might do better is they were positioned more clearly on the thirds lines instead of so close to the outside edge.<br/> <br/>Exposure<br/> <br/>I am sure this was difficult to expose correctly.  The blown out highlights from the bulbs detract.  This would have had to be caught in the camera.<br/> <br/>The image has good contrast and color.  If you only did one thing, I would say straighten the image.<br/> <br/>Please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Ken<br/>alexzen<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) First I commend for trying something out of the box.   A few things that I notice: Composition The composition is not very interesting.  The line in the middle is not straight and that detracts.  I would straighten the image via crop.   The lights might do better is they were positioned more clearly on the thirds lines instead of so close to the outside edge. Exposure I am sure this was difficult to expose correctly.  The blown out highlights from the bulbs detract.  This would have had to be caught in the camera. The image has good contrast and color.  If you only did one thing, I would say straighten the image. Please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Kenalexzen ', '2007-12-11 19:17:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4309099, 616909, 70036, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Composition<br/> <br/>Very nice positioning of the apples.  The image is begging for more negative space, I believe.  The black space on the left is less than on the right.  If you gave the apples some room to breathe I think the image would be stronger.<br/> <br/>Focus<br/> <br/>Great focus and sharpness on the water droplets.   The water drops really make this image since the surface of the apples alone are not very intersting.<br/> <br/>Great color.<br/> <br/>What would I improve upon?   The image does very well until it gets down to the middle of the green apple.  There is some darkness on the front of the green apple, and more so in the reflection that I do not understand.  Not a shadow since it appears you used two lights.  <br/> <br/>The reflection has less focus, as it should, but it detracts a bit from the overall image.  The apples in the reflection are as big as the main subjects but lack the crisp focus and nice water drops.  So the reflections do compete a bit.<br/> <br/>Two things that might make this stronger:<br/> <br/>- leave more negative space<br/>- shoot from a higher angle so that the reflected apples are not as big and allow the main objects to anchor the image more.<br/> <br/>But, otherwise a very nice concept, good execution and good post processing.<br/> <br/>Please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Ken <br/>alexzen<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Composition Very nice positioning of the apples.  The image is begging for more negative space, I believe.  The black space on the left is less than on the right.  If you gave the apples some room to breathe I think the image would be stronger. Focus Great focus and sharpness on the water droplets.   The water drops really make this image since the surface of the apples alone are not very intersting. Great color. What would I improve upon?   The image does very well until it gets down to the middle of the green apple.  There is some darkness on the front of the green apple, and more so in the reflection that I do not understand.  Not a shadow since it appears you used two lights.   The reflection has less focus, as it should, but it detracts a bit from the overall image.  The apples in the reflection are as big as the main subjects but lack the crisp focus and nice water drops.  So the reflections do compete a bit. Two things that might make this stronger: - leave more negative space- shoot from a higher angle so that the reflected apples are not as big and allow the main objects to anchor the image more. But, otherwise a very nice concept, good execution and good post processing. Please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Ken alexzen ', '2007-12-11 20:30:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4309344, 615561, 80096, '<td valign="top">Thanks Chuck! I must have done something right this time...finally! ;-)</td>', 'Thanks Chuck! I must have done something right this time...finally! ;-)', '2007-12-11 23:41:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4310873, 617351, 77425, '<td valign="top">I just stumbled across this image. Constructive Comments- Try not to take a picture like this from straight above. This is how we ALWAYS see dice. Your aperture setting at 14 brings the whole image in focus. try setting your aperture as high (low number) as you can so that the background is blurred, the focus should be on the dice. the used dice also hurt the image. the scuffs on the top don''t help. Old can work, but its gotta be really old. And try moving the light around, some long shadows may have helped this image.<br/>Good luck in future challenges.<br/> <br/></td>', 'I just stumbled across this image. Constructive Comments- Try not to take a picture like this from straight above. This is how we ALWAYS see dice. Your aperture setting at 14 brings the whole image in focus. try setting your aperture as high (low number) as you can so that the background is blurred, the focus should be on the dice. the used dice also hurt the image. the scuffs on the top don''t help. Old can work, but its gotta be really old. And try moving the light around, some long shadows may have helped this image.Good luck in future challenges. ', '2007-12-12 12:06:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4314576, 617351, 86896, '<td valign="top">Thanks.  I kinda thought that when submitted the picture.  I just was not being very creative at the time and could not think of anything else.  <br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ZeppKash:</b></div><hr/><i> I just stumbled across this image. Constructive Comments- Try not to take a picture like this from straight above. This is how we ALWAYS see dice. Your aperture setting at 14 brings the whole image in focus. try setting your aperture as high (low number) as you can so that the background is blurred, the focus should be on the dice. the used dice also hurt the image. the scuffs on the top don''t help. Old can work, but its gotta be really old. And try moving the light around, some long shadows may have helped this image.<br/>Good luck in future challenges. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Thanks.  I kinda thought that when submitted the picture.  I just was not being very creative at the time and could not think of anything else.   Originally posted by ZeppKash: I just stumbled across this image. Constructive Comments- Try not to take a picture like this from straight above. This is how we ALWAYS see dice. Your aperture setting at 14 brings the whole image in focus. try setting your aperture as high (low number) as you can so that the background is blurred, the focus should be on the dice. the used dice also hurt the image. the scuffs on the top don''t help. Old can work, but its gotta be really old. And try moving the light around, some long shadows may have helped this image.Good luck in future challenges. ', '2007-12-14 12:02:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4321258, 617413, 31637, '<td valign="top">This is a fantastic shot. The composition is very good. Who snapped the shot? Neighbors look at me funny too, especially when I set my timer and pose myself! Great finish for this.</td>', 'This is a fantastic shot. The composition is very good. Who snapped the shot? Neighbors look at me funny too, especially when I set my timer and pose myself! Great finish for this.', '2007-12-18 19:09:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4322299, 616912, 51793, '<td valign="top">This really is an outstanding caputre. It''s a shame that this only got a 5.5. Maybe because it was in the wrong challenge. Try it again in a free study for Dec, You have to score better than a 5.5, you got robbed.</td>', 'This really is an outstanding caputre. It''s a shame that this only got a 5.5. Maybe because it was in the wrong challenge. Try it again in a free study for Dec, You have to score better than a 5.5, you got robbed.', '2007-12-19 07:06:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4324898, 616374, 60862, '<td valign="top">Nice composition. :)<br/> <br/>It definitely looks too sharp.  That can happen when you have very small details like in the reeds.  Just don''t sharpen it as much, or lower the default sharpening setting on your camera.<br/> <br/>As you can tell from the comments, you can''t please everyone on color.  Some wanted less red, some wanted more blue.  Just do what you like and accept it won''t hit home universally.<br/> <br/>The final aspect of scoring high is nailing the challenge, and you didn''t quite get it right with this color combo.  The key is to learn when your score reflected missing the challenge vs. not being a great photo.  FWIW, I''ve been in many more challenges, and I still often miss the point voters are looking for.</td>', 'Nice composition. :) It definitely looks too sharp.  That can happen when you have very small details like in the reeds.  Just don''t sharpen it as much, or lower the default sharpening setting on your camera. As you can tell from the comments, you can''t please everyone on color.  Some wanted less red, some wanted more blue.  Just do what you like and accept it won''t hit home universally. The final aspect of scoring high is nailing the challenge, and you didn''t quite get it right with this color combo.  The key is to learn when your score reflected missing the challenge vs. not being a great photo.  FWIW, I''ve been in many more challenges, and I still often miss the point voters are looking for.', '2007-12-19 22:59:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4325037, 616374, 80859, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by levyj413:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice composition. :)<br/> <br/>It definitely looks too sharp.  That can happen when you have very small details like in the reeds.  Just don''t sharpen it as much, or lower the default sharpening setting on your camera.<br/> <br/>As you can tell from the comments, you can''t please everyone on color.  Some wanted less red, some wanted more blue.  Just do what you like and accept it won''t hit home universally.<br/> <br/>The final aspect of scoring high is nailing the challenge, and you didn''t quite get it right with this color combo.  The key is to learn when your score reflected missing the challenge vs. not being a great photo.  FWIW, I''ve been in many more challenges, and I still often miss the point voters are looking for. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>i thought the ''red'' was orange. orange/blue was what i was going for as my comp colors.  maybe i saturated it too much.  <br/> <br/>i don''t know how i got the sharpness.  this has happened to me before.  (i have taken self portraits and my very ''fine'' hair has come out looking like those reeds.)  the only thing i did to it that had anything to do with sharpness was use the ''unsharp mask'' that was suggested in something i read on this site and i don''t even know what that does.  i''ve got a lot to figure out and you have been a great help tonight.</td>', 'Originally posted by levyj413: Nice composition. :) It definitely looks too sharp.  That can happen when you have very small details like in the reeds.  Just don''t sharpen it as much, or lower the default sharpening setting on your camera. As you can tell from the comments, you can''t please everyone on color.  Some wanted less red, some wanted more blue.  Just do what you like and accept it won''t hit home universally. The final aspect of scoring high is nailing the challenge, and you didn''t quite get it right with this color combo.  The key is to learn when your score reflected missing the challenge vs. not being a great photo.  FWIW, I''ve been in many more challenges, and I still often miss the point voters are looking for.   i thought the ''red'' was orange. orange/blue was what i was going for as my comp colors.  maybe i saturated it too much.   i don''t know how i got the sharpness.  this has happened to me before.  (i have taken self portraits and my very ''fine'' hair has come out looking like those reeds.)  the only thing i did to it that had anything to do with sharpness was use the ''unsharp mask'' that was suggested in something i read on this site and i don''t even know what that does.  i''ve got a lot to figure out and you have been a great help tonight.', '2007-12-19 23:59:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4325839, 616374, 15711, '<td valign="top">Love scene.  I love intense colors, but the reds and yellows are just a touch oversaturrated for my taste. Maybe deepen the sky color to balance it out a smidge.  Wonderful composition.</td>', 'Love scene.  I love intense colors, but the reds and yellows are just a touch oversaturrated for my taste. Maybe deepen the sky color to balance it out a smidge.  Wonderful composition.', '2007-12-20 11:18:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4329687, 616122, 88010, '<td valign="top">I''m new here and I find many of the shots here inspirational getting me back in the mood to get the camera out more often. Very nice idea and good execution .</td>', 'I''m new here and I find many of the shots here inspirational getting me back in the mood to get the camera out more often. Very nice idea and good execution .', '2007-12-22 10:02:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4330631, 617383, 60862, '<td valign="top">The more I look at this, the more I appreciated the flowing lines and wild colors.  I''d suggest cloning out the non-black stuff in the upper right, though, to make it a pure background.  I''d also either sharpen it more or blur it more.  It''s kind of in-between right now.</td>', 'The more I look at this, the more I appreciated the flowing lines and wild colors.  I''d suggest cloning out the non-black stuff in the upper right, though, to make it a pure background.  I''d also either sharpen it more or blur it more.  It''s kind of in-between right now.', '2007-12-22 23:30:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4330634, 617097, 60862, '<td valign="top">Your style is clear here.  I can appreciate shots like this, as Melethia knows, but I find myself wanting more contrast and sharp distinctions.  The shot as framed works for me, but I''d do some things differently in editing.</td>', 'Your style is clear here.  I can appreciate shots like this, as Melethia knows, but I find myself wanting more contrast and sharp distinctions.  The shot as framed works for me, but I''d do some things differently in editing.', '2007-12-22 23:32:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4330635, 617185, 60862, '<td valign="top">I really like the colors and composition.  The glow behind the mountain doesn''t phase me, but the fact it follows the silo''s edges jars me as an editing artifact.</td>', 'I really like the colors and composition.  The glow behind the mountain doesn''t phase me, but the fact it follows the silo''s edges jars me as an editing artifact.', '2007-12-22 23:34:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4330637, 617376, 60862, '<td valign="top">I love the composition and shapes.  My tastes run to higher contrast, though.  Play around with it and see if you like it better - ramp up the contrast using various tools like curves, levels, and even just the brightness/contrast sliders.  Also try USM set to something like 20, 50, 0.  USM can create sharper contrast along edges while not blowing highlights or dropping out shadowed areas.  I''d also bump up the saturation.</td>', 'I love the composition and shapes.  My tastes run to higher contrast, though.  Play around with it and see if you like it better - ramp up the contrast using various tools like curves, levels, and even just the brightness/contrast sliders.  Also try USM set to something like 20, 50, 0.  USM can create sharper contrast along edges while not blowing highlights or dropping out shadowed areas.  I''d also bump up the saturation.', '2007-12-22 23:36:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4330639, 617299, 60862, '<td valign="top">Well, you called it:  abstracts rarely do well here.  But I LOVE IT.  The composition is wonderful, driving me to the one light in front.  The colors are fun and bold, and I like the blurry/painterly feel to it.  In fact, it''s going in my faves. :)  I could see this on a card.</td>', 'Well, you called it:  abstracts rarely do well here.  But I LOVE IT.  The composition is wonderful, driving me to the one light in front.  The colors are fun and bold, and I like the blurry/painterly feel to it.  In fact, it''s going in my faves. :)  I could see this on a card.', '2007-12-22 23:38:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4330640, 617485, 60862, '<td valign="top">Well, with no prep and no effort, you did okay.  I''d suggest brightening it up a bit, but ultimately, the subject doesn''t hold my interest long.</td>', 'Well, with no prep and no effort, you did okay.  I''d suggest brightening it up a bit, but ultimately, the subject doesn''t hold my interest long.', '2007-12-22 23:40:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4330642, 617476, 60862, '<td valign="top">Centered, a tree coming out of her head (well, skewering her right through) - you do like to poke fingers in the eyes of the rulemongers, doncha? ;)</td>', 'Centered, a tree coming out of her head (well, skewering her right through) - you do like to poke fingers in the eyes of the rulemongers, doncha? ;)', '2007-12-22 23:41:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4330646, 617343, 60862, '<td valign="top">Nice colors, but it looks more like graphic art to me than a photo.  I mean, I know it''s a photo, of course. :)</td>', 'Nice colors, but it looks more like graphic art to me than a photo.  I mean, I know it''s a photo, of course. :)', '2007-12-22 23:42:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(4339239, 617445, 83313, '<td valign="top">I just happened across this image again while browsing and noticed that you did it with a point and shoot. I''m even more impressed. More proof that the talent of the photographer is more important than the gear.</td>', 'I just happened across this image again while browsing and noticed that you did it with a point and shoot. I''m even more impressed. More proof that the talent of the photographer is more important than the gear.', '2007-12-27 17:46:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4346518, 616374, 83313, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote on the challenge this was in, but it''s really nice. Nice crisp colors. this is one of those shots that could have benefited from more resolution allowed in a challenge.</td>', 'I didn''t vote on the challenge this was in, but it''s really nice. Nice crisp colors. this is one of those shots that could have benefited from more resolution allowed in a challenge.', '2007-12-31 01:01:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(4352023, 617492, 67697, '<td valign="top">Great idea!  This does make you think for a bit.  Took me a minute but I can see the inside and outside now lol.</td>', 'Great idea!  This does make you think for a bit.  Took me a minute but I can see the inside and outside now lol.', '2008-01-01 23:50:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4356243, 615595, 82707, '<td valign="top">Great colours, love the detail.</td>', 'Great colours, love the detail.', '2008-01-03 01:35:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(4357515, 617390, 70000, '<td valign="top">Oh the colors are awesome, I would like to see a little deeper depth of field</td>', 'Oh the colors are awesome, I would like to see a little deeper depth of field', '2008-01-03 13:39:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4361015, 616191, 86895, '<td valign="top">My two favorite complimentary colors!  I wouldn''t have guessed this to be coleus.  It''s a great photo!<br/> <br/>p.s. make all the comments you want.  I need some feedback other than my mum telling me my pictures are pretty. :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-01-04 17:32:49.</i></td>', 'My two favorite complimentary colors!  I wouldn''t have guessed this to be coleus.  It''s a great photo! p.s. make all the comments you want.  I need some feedback other than my mum telling me my pictures are pretty. :)', '2008-01-04 17:31:53.000000', '2008-01-04 17:32:49.000000', 0),
(4366636, 617187, 71538, '<td valign="top">Wow! everything is perfect in this picture, depth of field, composition, colours!!!</td>', 'Wow! everything is perfect in this picture, depth of field, composition, colours!!!', '2008-01-06 15:51:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4383961, 617100, 78020, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by srdanz:</b></div><hr/><i> Vec pokazujes napredak... mislim da su u pravu ovi koji su rekli da je "burned out" - desni cosak i jeste malo ''overexposed'' - ali je zgleda tako moralo biti obzirom na to da sama ruza izgleda korektno osvijetljena. <br/>Kako izbjeci ovo ubuduce? Najjednostavniji nacin je da se zakloni necim izvor svjetla (sunce) na onom presvijetlom dijelu. Alternativa je da se dodatno osvijetli sam objekat, i u isto vrijeme smanji vrijeme ekspozicije. Npr. mozes koristiti blic.<br/> <br/>Druga stvar je nesto sto se zove rule of thirds - a u stvari se radi o zlatnom presjeku. Potrazi malo po interetu (ili u knjigama matematike :-) o tome, pa mozes sam testirati teoriju da je ljudskom oku privlacnije kada se objekti ne nalaze u centru fotografije, nego kad su malo smaknuti (<a href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_ratio" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">link</a>)<br/> <br/>Probaj odrezati donji desni kraj tako da se centar ruze pomjeri prema donjem desnom cosku, oko 1/3 odozdo i s desna, i vidi kako ti se vizuelno cini.<br/> <br/>Sretno ubuduce!<br/> <br/>-Srdjan </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hvala za savjete, ali na ovoj sici svi govore da je ruza previse centrirana, a sad imam sliku klovna i neko mi je rekao da treba biti vise centriran klovn. Kako cu znati kad treba da bude centriran a kad ne treba?</td>', 'Originally posted by srdanz: Vec pokazujes napredak... mislim da su u pravu ovi koji su rekli da je "burned out" - desni cosak i jeste malo ''overexposed'' - ali je zgleda tako moralo biti obzirom na to da sama ruza izgleda korektno osvijetljena. Kako izbjeci ovo ubuduce? Najjednostavniji nacin je da se zakloni necim izvor svjetla (sunce) na onom presvijetlom dijelu. Alternativa je da se dodatno osvijetli sam objekat, i u isto vrijeme smanji vrijeme ekspozicije. Npr. mozes koristiti blic. Druga stvar je nesto sto se zove rule of thirds - a u stvari se radi o zlatnom presjeku. Potrazi malo po interetu (ili u knjigama matematike :-) o tome, pa mozes sam testirati teoriju da je ljudskom oku privlacnije kada se objekti ne nalaze u centru fotografije, nego kad su malo smaknuti (link) Probaj odrezati donji desni kraj tako da se centar ruze pomjeri prema donjem desnom cosku, oko 1/3 odozdo i s desna, i vidi kako ti se vizuelno cini. Sretno ubuduce! -Srdjan   Hvala za savjete, ali na ovoj sici svi govore da je ruza previse centrirana, a sad imam sliku klovna i neko mi je rekao da treba biti vise centriran klovn. Kako cu znati kad treba da bude centriran a kad ne treba?', '2008-01-11 04:45:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4392259, 617449, 48228, '<td valign="top">Excellent images and a good result for this bright colored, well focused, well designed shot.....</td>', 'Excellent images and a good result for this bright colored, well focused, well designed shot.....', '2008-01-14 20:08:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4422413, 616573, 49804, '<td valign="top">Awesome shot, nailed the composition as well as the focus, great colors and contrast, very nicely done, and congrats on the good score.</td>', 'Awesome shot, nailed the composition as well as the focus, great colors and contrast, very nicely done, and congrats on the good score.', '2008-01-24 18:21:33.000000', NULL, 0),
